WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:02.580
“Remember, Remember, the Fifth of November.

00:00:02.580 --> 00:00:04.960
The Gunpowder Treason, and Plot.

00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:16.470
I know of know reason why the Gunpowder Treason
should ever be forgot.”

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:20.980
On November the 5th, 1604, thirteen men plotted
together to blow up the Palace of Westminster

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:25.590
in London on the day when the most powerful
men in England were set to meet at Parliament.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:29.519
The authorities learned about the plan through
an anonymous letter, and the terrorists were

00:00:29.519 --> 00:00:31.589
stopped just in time.

00:00:31.589 --> 00:00:35.840
The first man they encountered at the scene
was Guy Fawkes, who had been guarding barrels

00:00:35.840 --> 00:00:38.480
of gunpowder in the basement below the palace.

00:00:38.480 --> 00:00:42.910
If you’re an American, you probably know
about Guy Fawkes from the movie V for Vendetta,

00:00:42.910 --> 00:00:45.620
and you most likely associate him with anarchy.

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:49.770
This association has been pushed even more
in recent years with the use of Guy Fawkes

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:51.370
masks by the Anonymous organization.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:55.340
If you’re from the UK, you already know
about Guy Fawkes Night, which is celebrated

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.890
every November 5th with a bonfire and fireworks.

00:00:58.890 --> 00:01:04.530
Nearly everyone has heard of the famous Gunpowder
Plot, but few people know the details about

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:09.220
Guy Fawke’s life, or the motivations behind
why he and his friends wanted to blow up Parliament

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.420
in the first place.

00:01:10.420 --> 00:01:16.890
Even though this is a biography of his life,
Guy Fawkes is a very small part in this larger

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:17.890
story.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:22.170
In order to fully understand the motivations
behind the Gunpowder Plot, we first need to

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:27.970
explain the conflicts between English Catholics
and Protestants at that time.

00:01:27.970 --> 00:01:32.900
So, What’s Up With The Catholics?

00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:37.310
For a large part of human history, the most
powerful religion in the world was the Roman

00:01:37.310 --> 00:01:38.310
Catholic Church.

00:01:38.310 --> 00:01:43.380
If a country was Catholic, its citizens looked
up to the reigning Pope as their religious

00:01:43.380 --> 00:01:48.770
leader, and in the minds of some, this authority
was more important than their loyalty to their

00:01:48.770 --> 00:01:54.060
actual King of Queen because whoever has access
to God has access to your mortal soul.

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:59.210
In a lot of ways, the Protestant Reformation
was a way to remove all of the power being

00:01:59.210 --> 00:02:01.080
held by the Popes and Bishops.

00:02:01.080 --> 00:02:05.270
It was sort of like cutting out the middleman
for the average person’s access to God.

00:02:05.270 --> 00:02:08.971
Because, you see, Catholics are taught that
if you want your sins to be forgiven, you

00:02:08.971 --> 00:02:12.570
have to tell a priest every bad thing you
have ever done in confession.

00:02:12.570 --> 00:02:15.790
A priest is sworn to secrecy, kind of like
a therapist.

00:02:15.790 --> 00:02:20.090
But even so, everyone had the knowledge that
these men held all of the deepest darkest

00:02:20.090 --> 00:02:22.520
secrets of their congregation.

00:02:22.520 --> 00:02:24.530
Confession wasn’t just encouraged.

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.680
It’s mandatory.

00:02:25.680 --> 00:02:29.070
And even the smallest sin left unsaid could
mean you’re going to Hell.

00:02:29.070 --> 00:02:33.800
On top of that, Catholic mass was said in
Latin, so everyone needed to study the language.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.430
For the uneducated peasants, they needed to
rely on a translation from their priest.

00:02:38.430 --> 00:02:42.450
Basically, the religion is set up in such
a way where priests and the Pope were given

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:45.100
a huge amount of power over their congregation.

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:49.440
In 1558, Elizabeth declared that there should
be a “settlement”, which declared that

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:52.920
all English citizens must convert to Protestantism.

00:02:52.920 --> 00:02:57.800
Bishops that were formerly apart of the Catholic
Church must renounce their loyalty to the

00:02:57.800 --> 00:02:59.470
Pope, if they wanted to live.

00:02:59.470 --> 00:03:04.070
It was now mandatory for every English person
to go to Protestant church services every

00:03:04.070 --> 00:03:06.550
Sunday, and they were taking attendance.

00:03:06.550 --> 00:03:11.020
If anyone missed one too many services, they
were fined, or sent to jail.

00:03:11.020 --> 00:03:14.930
After hearing this, Pope Pius V excommunicated
Elizabeth from the Catholic Church.

00:03:14.930 --> 00:03:20.830
In 1570, he commanded a papal bull that encouraged
all Catholics to depose her- Basically, do

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:22.740
not be loyal to their Queen.

00:03:22.740 --> 00:03:27.490
He called her "Elizabeth, the pretended Queen
of England, and the servant of crime".

00:03:27.490 --> 00:03:30.440
You can probably see why this was problematic.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:33.610
Catholics were now seen as enemy agents.

00:03:33.610 --> 00:03:36.250
People in the lower classes were quick to
convert to Protestantism.

00:03:36.250 --> 00:03:40.160
They could not afford to pay the hefty fines,
and many of the illiterate peasants couldn’t

00:03:40.160 --> 00:03:41.500
speak or read Latin, anyway.

00:03:41.500 --> 00:03:44.990
So it was an easy choice to make, and a symbol
that they were loyal to their Queen.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:49.290
But for the educated people of the upper class,
this was not such an easy conversion.

00:03:49.290 --> 00:03:53.120
For one thing, this was taking away the freedom
to choose their religion, and there were plenty

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:58.210
of people who still truly believe that the
Catholic Church was the one true church.

00:03:58.210 --> 00:04:03.170
These people were called “recusants”,
which comes from the Latin word recusare,

00:04:03.170 --> 00:04:04.610
which means “to refuse”.

00:04:04.610 --> 00:04:09.290
For these people who broke the law and continued
to practice their Catholic faith, they believed

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:13.280
they were fighting for their immortal souls.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:18.580
Since so much of the religion relies on a
priest to say mass and give confession, recusant

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:21.190
Catholics began to hide priests in their home.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:25.310
This was completely illegal, and harboring
a priest was punishable by death.

00:04:25.310 --> 00:04:28.770
If it was known at a family was Catholic,
the royal guard would show up unannounced

00:04:28.770 --> 00:04:32.890
at all times of the day and night to ransack
their homes, looking for hidden priests.

00:04:32.890 --> 00:04:36.950
Upper-class Catholic families who refused
to attend Protestant mass continued to pay

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:41.100
expensive fines, to the point where they were
losing all of their family inheritance.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:45.040
Many English Catholics were forced to move
to Flanders, which was a safe zone.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:49.450
After Elizabeth I’s death, the Scottish
King James VI took over the throne, and became

00:04:49.450 --> 00:04:51.210
King James I of England.

00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:55.080
Catholic citizens had no idea how his reign
would be any different than Elizabeth’s

00:04:55.080 --> 00:05:03.960
and they waited to see what would happen next.

00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:04.960
The Life of Guy Fawkes

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:08.770
There is not very much known about Guy Fawkes’
childhood, either, except that he was born

00:05:08.770 --> 00:05:13.220
in 1570 in York, England to Edward and Edith
Fawkes.

00:05:13.220 --> 00:05:17.330
His family had been Protestant, and his father
even worked for The Church of England.

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:20.960
They were law-abiding Protestants who went
to church every Sunday.

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:25.570
His mother came from along line of Catholics,
but she chose to give up her faith in favor

00:05:25.570 --> 00:05:26.570
of conforming.

00:05:26.570 --> 00:05:31.210
Guy Fawke’s father died when he was 8 years
old, and his mother was a widow for years

00:05:31.210 --> 00:05:33.670
before she decided to marry a Catholic man.

00:05:33.670 --> 00:05:37.940
They began practicing the faith in secret,
and they baptized Guy and his siblings in

00:05:37.940 --> 00:05:41.180
a secret ceremony in the St. Michael le Belfrey
church.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:45.220
He attended St. Peter’s School in York,
which had a lot of recusant Catholic teachers

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:46.220
and students.

00:05:46.220 --> 00:05:49.270
He was able to attend mass in the homes of
people who were hiding priests.

00:05:49.270 --> 00:05:53.520
As an adult, he chose to continue practicing
that Catholic faith, and he became passionate

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:55.510
about trying to help protect it.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:05:58.670
At some point, Guy Fawkes is said to have
gotten married and had a son.

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:03.860
There are records from 1590 that a man named
Guy Fawkes married a woman named Maria Pulleyn,

00:06:03.860 --> 00:06:07.800
and a birth certificate of their son, Thomas
Fawkes.

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:12.600
When he was 21 years old, he would have been
old enough to take out his inheritance.

00:06:12.600 --> 00:06:18.400
That same year, there are documents of a lease
of a 3-and-a-half-acre piece of land and home

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:23.450
signed by Guy Fawkes, including a stamp with
the image of a falcon, which was on his family

00:06:23.450 --> 00:06:24.450
crest.

00:06:24.450 --> 00:06:25.450
He once had a very normal life.

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:28.350
He entered the service of Anthony Brown, 1st
Viscount of Montagu as a footman.

00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:32.200
At that time, working in the service of a
Lord was considered to be a very respectable

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:35.430
job among the lower class, especially compared
to being a farmer.

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:40.010
But for whatever reason, Brown did not like
Guy Fawkes, so he fired him.

00:06:40.010 --> 00:06:43.280
Back then, your reputation was everything,
and it must have been difficult for him to

00:06:43.280 --> 00:06:45.970
get another job without a good letter of recommendation.

00:06:45.970 --> 00:06:49.900
He managed to work for Brown’s grandson
after Anthony Brown’s death.

00:06:49.900 --> 00:06:52.910
From the records, it would seem that he struggled
to maintain steady employment.

00:06:52.910 --> 00:06:56.730
So at 21 years old, he left England and move
to Flanders.

00:06:56.730 --> 00:07:00.500
He fought together with the Spanish army,
to do his part in the Eighty Year War.

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:05.020
At that time, Spain was considered to be the
protectors of the Catholic faith, and during

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:08.520
the war, they were fending off Dutch Protestantism
in the Netherlands.

00:07:08.520 --> 00:07:12.260
While fighting with the Spanish, he decided
to go by the name “Guido”.

00:07:12.260 --> 00:07:16.830
He was described by one of his compatriots
to be "of excellent good natural parts, very

00:07:16.830 --> 00:07:22.150
resolute and universally learned", and was
"sought by all the most distinguished in the

00:07:22.150 --> 00:07:25.120
Archduke's camp for nobility and virtue".

00:07:25.120 --> 00:07:27.760
People say that he was very tall and muscular.

00:07:27.760 --> 00:07:32.730
He had reddish-brown hair and beard, and was
basically described as being the perfect soldier.

00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:37.490
Despite having these descriptions, No one
knows what Guy Fawkes truly looks like, because

00:07:37.490 --> 00:07:39.890
there was never a portrait painted of his
likeness.

00:07:39.890 --> 00:07:43.960
We only have the caricatures that depicted
him after his death, and these were mostly

00:07:43.960 --> 00:07:46.530
drawn in such a way that made him look like
a villain.

00:07:46.530 --> 00:07:51.900
In most images, he has black hair and a beard
with an upturned mustache.

00:07:51.900 --> 00:07:59.699
The Gunpowder Plot
After King James I came into power, Catholics

00:07:59.699 --> 00:08:02.380
waited with bated breath to see what would
happen next.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:07.250
A recusant Catholic man named Thomas Percy
was a cousin of Henry Percy, the 9th Earl

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:08.380
of Northumberland.

00:08:08.380 --> 00:08:12.130
Even though he was not a Lord himself, Percy
was able to take it upon himself to request

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.430
an audience with the King.

00:08:13.430 --> 00:08:16.620
He asked for mercy on behalf of the English
Catholics.

00:08:16.620 --> 00:08:21.290
Wanting to gain popularity with his new English
subjects, James was vague, and made sure not

00:08:21.290 --> 00:08:22.470
to make any promises.

00:08:22.470 --> 00:08:26.150
It was still very early in his reign, and
he was not sure yet what he should do about

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:28.570
the tensions between Protestants and Catholics.

00:08:28.570 --> 00:08:33.349
He essentially told Percy not to worry, because
he personally had no ill will towards Catholics.

00:08:33.349 --> 00:08:36.849
Percy believed that King James was going to
offer some kind of relief, and that he might

00:08:36.849 --> 00:08:40.099
be getting ready to repeal Queen Elizabeth
I’s laws.

00:08:40.099 --> 00:08:43.300
Percy was very happy about this, and returned
to tell his friends and family that they no

00:08:43.300 --> 00:08:46.160
longer had to worry about being persecuted
for their faith any longer.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:51.339
Some even hoped that maybe James would convert
to Catholicism, and the entire country would

00:08:51.339 --> 00:08:54.530
revert back to practicing the one true church.

00:08:54.530 --> 00:08:58.020
For about a year, English Catholics were able
to live a normal life.

00:08:58.020 --> 00:09:02.120
James temporarily stopped collecting fees
that recusant Catholics were required to pay

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.250
for skipping Protestant service.

00:09:04.250 --> 00:09:08.110
He also did not push for his guard to search
Catholic homes for harboring priests.

00:09:08.110 --> 00:09:11.180
However, the laws made by Elizabeth I were
still in place.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:15.490
He had not repealed them, because he was waiting
to see what the reaction would be from his

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:16.990
Protestant Parliament.

00:09:16.990 --> 00:09:20.950
In the summer of 1604, the members of Parliament
finally noticed that Catholics were not being

00:09:20.950 --> 00:09:25.010
persecuted anymore, and they began to push
King James to come down hard on them.

00:09:25.010 --> 00:09:29.190
The way they felt about Catholics was very
similar to Communists in the Cold War.

00:09:29.190 --> 00:09:32.750
Many of them believed that if they were not
stamped out, they would cause an uprising.

00:09:32.750 --> 00:09:36.750
So, James brought back the same laws the Elizabeth
I had put in place.

00:09:36.750 --> 00:09:40.310
Suddenly, Catholic homes were being searched
once again, and they were being treated like

00:09:40.310 --> 00:09:41.310
criminals.

00:09:41.310 --> 00:09:45.360
The Catholic people in England had lived so
long being oppressed, but the thing that triggered

00:09:45.360 --> 00:09:47.720
their anger was the sense of false hope.

00:09:47.720 --> 00:09:52.670
They felt betrayed by King James, and it was
enough to make some want to kill him.

00:09:52.670 --> 00:09:56.670
Even though Guy Fawkes is the one who is most
remembered for the Gunpowder Plot, the ring

00:09:56.670 --> 00:09:59.850
leader was actually a man named Robert Catesby.

00:09:59.850 --> 00:10:04.500
He began making plans in 1603, and first recruited
a man named Thomas Winter.

00:10:04.500 --> 00:10:08.910
Catesby and Winter rode to Spain, because
they had associates who were Catholic.

00:10:08.910 --> 00:10:12.730
Spain was also designated as the protectors
of the Catholic faith.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.720
Since Catholics in England were being persecuted
once again, they begged for help from the

00:10:15.720 --> 00:10:18.830
Spanish to stop King James from killing their
people.

00:10:18.830 --> 00:10:22.860
However, the Spanish were not interested in
getting involved.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:26.400
Catesby and Winter returned to England, and
decided if they were going to find anyone

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.570
to help them, it would have to be at home.

00:10:28.570 --> 00:10:31.830
They found John Wright, and Thomas Percy.

00:10:31.830 --> 00:10:35.779
Winter had gone to school with Guy Fawkes,
and he seemed like the perfect candidate to

00:10:35.779 --> 00:10:37.089
help them with the plot.

00:10:37.089 --> 00:10:41.550
After all, Fawkes had plenty of experience
fighting in Spain, and he knew a lot about

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:42.550
gunpowder.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:45.620
He was smart, and knew how to stay cool under
pressure.

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:50.130
In May of 1604, the five men were spotted
together at London’s Duck and Drake Inn.

00:10:50.130 --> 00:10:53.800
They whispered about their plot, and swore
an oath of loyalty and secrecy.

00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.980
The group was biding their time, trying to
figure out the finer details of the plan as

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:58.980
time went on.

00:10:58.980 --> 00:11:02.520
Thomas Percy had the resources to purchased
a property in London that was very close to

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:03.910
The Palace of Westminster.

00:11:03.910 --> 00:11:07.589
Guy Fawkes began to live with him, posing
as a footman named “John Johnson”.

00:11:07.589 --> 00:11:11.240
This way, they would never seem out of the
ordinary to anyone who witnessed them around

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:12.240
town.

00:11:12.240 --> 00:11:15.980
At that time, it was not uncommon for men
to buy gunpowder, especially if they planned

00:11:15.980 --> 00:11:17.110
to sail overseas.

00:11:17.110 --> 00:11:21.560
They needed the powder to use their guns and
cannons to defend themselves from pirates.

00:11:21.560 --> 00:11:27.050
The only trouble was buying small quantities
over a long period of time, as not to raise

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:28.050
suspicions.

00:11:28.050 --> 00:11:32.180
Guy Fawkes would use his connections to slowly
gather a cache of gunpowder barrels that were

00:11:32.180 --> 00:11:36.030
leftover from ships entering the harbor, and
bringing them back to Thomas Percy.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:39.839
At the time, the Palace of Westminster had
a collection of smaller buildings.

00:11:39.839 --> 00:11:42.870
Lords and other members of the upper class
would come and go from those buildings on

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:45.670
a regular basis without being stopped by security.

00:11:45.670 --> 00:11:49.900
The rules were very relaxed, and it was actually
easy for Thomas Percy to rent a storage space

00:11:49.900 --> 00:11:54.839
in the basement below the Palace, claiming
that it was for his cousin, The Earl of Northumberland,

00:11:54.839 --> 00:11:56.540
to store his firewood for winter.

00:11:56.540 --> 00:12:00.950
The day of Parliament kept getting delayed,
and the group of conspirators grew from 5

00:12:00.950 --> 00:12:01.950
to 13 men.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:05.670
Unfortuantely for them, though, the extended
time combined with the greater number of people

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:09.700
who were being told about the plot meant that
it was far more likely that the secret was

00:12:09.700 --> 00:12:10.700
going to get out.

00:12:10.700 --> 00:12:15.339
A Catholic man named Lord Monteagle was preparing
to be present at Parliament.

00:12:15.339 --> 00:12:19.880
A masked man handed a letter to one of Monteagle
servants, and it was presented to him immediately.

00:12:19.880 --> 00:12:25.110
It said; “My lord, out of the love I bear
to some of your friends, I have a care of

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:29.580
your preservation, therefore I would advise
you as you tender your life to devise some

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:33.970
excuse to shift of your attendance at this
parliament . . . for though there be no appearance

00:12:33.970 --> 00:12:38.850
of any stir, yet I say they shall receive
a terrible blow.”

00:12:38.850 --> 00:12:42.240
Even though it was late at night, Lord Monteagle
quickly told his servants to ready the horses,

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:46.820
so that he could deliver the letter to Robert
Cecil, the Spy Master and Secretary of State

00:12:46.820 --> 00:12:48.320
to King James.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:51.940
Historians have debated over the theories
of who actually wrote that anonymous letter.

00:12:51.940 --> 00:12:53.890
It could have been one of the 13 conspirators.

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:58.360
It may have even been Lord Monteagle himself,
writing a fake letter after hearing letters

00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:00.730
through the Catholic recusant grapevine.

00:13:00.730 --> 00:13:04.610
He was awarded 500 pounds per year for his
loyalty to the crown.

00:13:04.610 --> 00:13:07.010
Back then, that was a small fortune.

00:13:07.010 --> 00:13:09.460
Even more historian believe it was Robert
Cecil.

00:13:09.460 --> 00:13:13.500
He was the spy master, after all, and some
believe that he knew about the Gunpowder Plot

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:18.740
for a long time, and orchestrated the entire
scene to make himself seem like the hero.

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:21.890
On the 4th of November, there was an extensive
search of the Palace of Westminster.

00:13:21.890 --> 00:13:25.760
At first, they did not find anything that
concerned them, and they were beginning to

00:13:25.760 --> 00:13:27.390
believe that the letter was a hoax.

00:13:27.390 --> 00:13:30.930
But later that day, it was brought to the
royal guard’s attention that there were

00:13:30.930 --> 00:13:33.790
cellars underneath the palace that had not
been searched yet.

00:13:33.790 --> 00:13:37.680
A royal official named Sir Thomas Knyvett
was told that one of them was being used for

00:13:37.680 --> 00:13:41.540
storing firewood, so he lead a group of royal
guards to search the area.

00:13:41.540 --> 00:13:44.670
When they arrived, they found Guy Fawkes guarding
the firewood.

00:13:44.670 --> 00:13:49.209
Instead of wearing the clothes of a watchman,
Fawkes was dressed in his riding boots, spurs,

00:13:49.209 --> 00:13:53.250
hat, and cloak, as if he was getting ready
to jump on a horse at any moment.

00:13:53.250 --> 00:13:57.339
They moved the wood piles aside to reveal
36 barrels of gunpowder.

00:13:57.339 --> 00:14:00.990
The royal guards searched him and found a
box of long matches.

00:14:00.990 --> 00:14:02.610
Fawkes was immediately arrested.

00:14:02.610 --> 00:14:05.860
On November the 6th, King James wanted to
meet Guy Fawkes face-to-face.

00:14:05.860 --> 00:14:08.540
He interviewed him, asking if he had any regret.

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:13.300
He genuinely wanted to know how anyone could
be so ruthless to be willing to kill so many

00:14:13.300 --> 00:14:16.860
people- even the young children who would
have been present at Parliament.

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:20.470
Fawkes said that his only regret was that
the plan failed.

00:14:20.470 --> 00:14:23.750
Fawks still called himself “John Johnson”,
and he refused to give up the names of his

00:14:23.750 --> 00:14:24.959
co-conspirators.

00:14:24.959 --> 00:14:28.200
King James ordered that Fawkes be tortured
and interrogated.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:32.149
He was suspended by manacles, and then put
on the rack so that his arms and legs were

00:14:32.149 --> 00:14:34.610
stretched and popped out of their sockets.

00:14:34.610 --> 00:14:37.180
He eventually caved and gave his confession.

00:14:37.180 --> 00:14:41.149
In the before-and-after of his signature,
we can see that he could hardly write his

00:14:41.149 --> 00:14:44.269
own name, after enduring so much pain.

00:14:44.269 --> 00:14:47.970
While Guy Fawkes was being tortured, the rest
of the conspirators were on the run.

00:14:47.970 --> 00:14:52.820
Robert Catesby began to announce to the villages
that King James was dead, and he called for

00:14:52.820 --> 00:14:55.910
Catholics to rise up to reclaim their rightful
place in the kingdom.

00:14:55.910 --> 00:15:00.149
They rode from town to town, but instead of
the huge army he expected, there were only

00:15:00.149 --> 00:15:02.430
about 40 men who decided to follow him.

00:15:02.430 --> 00:15:06.600
Ironically, Catesby and his men accidently
blew themselves up with their own gunpowder

00:15:06.600 --> 00:15:08.100
they had brought with them.

00:15:08.100 --> 00:15:11.890
Without Guy Fawkes there to help them with
his expertise, they thought that in order

00:15:11.890 --> 00:15:16.650
to dry out the damp, they should sprinkle
their gunpowder in front of an open fireplace.

00:15:16.650 --> 00:15:20.120
It exploded, of course, and one of the men
had gone blind.

00:15:20.120 --> 00:15:22.080
The rest were now burned and injured.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:25.260
One of the men asked Robert Catesby what they
were going to do next.

00:15:25.260 --> 00:15:28.209
He replied, “We mean here to die.”

00:15:28.209 --> 00:15:32.190
On November the 8th, the sheriff of Warwickshire
showed up with a small army of 200 men.

00:15:32.190 --> 00:15:34.649
There was a shootout between the two groups.

00:15:34.649 --> 00:15:37.959
The weakened Catholic men did their best to
go out fighting, but it was clear that the

00:15:37.959 --> 00:15:40.079
king’s guard would overpowered them.

00:15:40.079 --> 00:15:43.450
Robert Catesby was shot, but crawled to the
nearby chapel.

00:15:43.450 --> 00:15:46.860
He was later found on the floor of the church,
hugging a statue of the Virgin Mary.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:51.980
The men who were left alive were taken prisoner,
and sentenced to hang in the gallows along

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:55.180
with Guy Fawkes.

00:15:55.180 --> 00:16:00.960
Death and Legacy
On the 31st of January, 1606, Guy Fawkes and

00:16:00.960 --> 00:16:04.210
his fellow conspirators were found guilty
of treason, and their punishment would have

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:06.540
been to “hanged, drawn, and quartered”.

00:16:06.540 --> 00:16:10.400
This meant that a man was dragged through
the streets before he was hanged in the gallows.

00:16:10.400 --> 00:16:13.720
But just before he was about to choke to death,
they would let him go.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:17.850
As he gasped for breath, they would dig a
knife into his stomach, and pull out his entrails.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:21.590
Then, they chopped off his arms and legs while
he was still alive.

00:16:21.590 --> 00:16:26.310
Then, the four quarters of their body were
taken to the four corners of England.

00:16:26.310 --> 00:16:30.680
As Guy Fawkes stood in front of the crowd,
King James declared that these Catholic traitors

00:16:30.680 --> 00:16:34.600
were trying to blow up the entire island of
England.

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:38.269
This would have been physically impossible,
of course, but it was enough to make people

00:16:38.269 --> 00:16:39.450
extremely angry.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:42.410
They were screaming and booing, calling him
a traitor.

00:16:42.410 --> 00:16:45.529
Before they could torture him again, Guy Fawkes
jumped, breaking his own neck.

00:16:45.529 --> 00:16:48.910
Even though he was no alive to feel the pain,
they still went through with cutting his body

00:16:48.910 --> 00:16:50.610
apart into pieces.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.770
The Gunpowder Plot had very nearly succeeded.

00:16:52.770 --> 00:16:56.519
And if it were not for the anonymous letter,
Guy Fawkes may have actually succeeded at

00:16:56.519 --> 00:16:57.660
lighting the fuse.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.070
If the barrels of gunpowder had exploded,
it would have been powerful enough to bring

00:17:01.070 --> 00:17:03.420
down the palace, and nearby buildings.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:07.049
It would have killed the King and the princes,
as well as some of the most powerful noblemen

00:17:07.049 --> 00:17:08.049
in the country.

00:17:08.049 --> 00:17:10.759
This would have left the throne to James’
daughter, Princess Elizabeth.

00:17:10.759 --> 00:17:15.199
They had hoped that since she was so young,
she would be easy to manipulate as a sort

00:17:15.199 --> 00:17:16.199
of puppet.

00:17:16.199 --> 00:17:19.470
Many believe that Robert Catesby would have
eventually gotten more Catholics to follow

00:17:19.470 --> 00:17:22.020
him, and this would have erupted into an English
civil war.

00:17:22.020 --> 00:17:25.959
After this incident, Parliament passed the
Thanksgiving Act of 1606, which was a law

00:17:25.959 --> 00:17:31.390
that English citizens must pray and give thanks
to God that the terrorists did not kill the

00:17:31.390 --> 00:17:32.390
King.

00:17:32.390 --> 00:17:35.600
That day became known as “Guy Fawkes Night”,
or “Bonfire Night”, and it is celebrated

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:37.509
every year on November the 5th.

00:17:37.509 --> 00:17:41.799
People usually celebrate by building a large
bonfire and burning a life-sized dummy of

00:17:41.799 --> 00:17:42.799
Guy Fawkes.

00:17:42.799 --> 00:17:47.230
There is also a fireworks show, to symbolize
the explosions that never happened.

00:17:47.230 --> 00:18:01.019
Since then, everyone has always remembered
the Fifth

00:18:01.019 --> 00:18:07.309
of November.

